language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ From the set A of ten integers, find two disjoint non-empty subsets S and T whose elements have equal sums.
given A : matrix indexed by [int(1..10)] of int
find in_S : matrix indexed by [int(1..10)] of bool
find in_T : matrix indexed by [int(1..10)] of bool

branching on [in_S, in_T]

such that
$ S is non-empty and T is non-empty
((exists i : int(1..10) . in_S[i]) /\ (exists i : int(1..10) . in_T[i])),
$ S and T are disjoint: no element of A is in both
forAll i : int(1..10) . !(in_S[i] /\ in_T[i]),
$ the elements of S and T have the same sum
(sum i : int(1..10) . toInt(in_S[i]) * A[i]) = (sum i : int(1..10) . toInt(in_T[i]) * A[i])
